course: dictionary
lesson: 3791
title: A footstool is for your feet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from two smaller words. Look for them, and the meaning often shows itself. Footstool is made of foot and stool. A stool is a seat with no back, and a foot is the part you walk on, so a footstool is a stool for your feet.
explain: «The Woman jumps onto a footstool and begs the Cat to eat it.» Here the footstool is in a room where the Woman sits. Jumping onto something means you are going up, so a footstool must be low enough to climb onto. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: a low seat for your feet fits.
explain: Some words also have a bigger meaning. In the Bible, God says «the earth is my footstool». Nobody puts their feet on the whole world. The words mean that God is so great that the whole earth is under his feet, as a sign of his power.
fact: A footstool is a low stool or small padded seat for resting your feet on.
fact: Footstool is made of two words: foot and stool.
fact: «The Woman jumps onto a footstool» tells you that a footstool is low enough to jump onto.
fact: In the Bible, «the earth is my footstool» means something under someone's feet, showing power.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The Woman jumps onto a footstool and begs the Cat to eat it.» What is a footstool? | A tall ladder for reaching high shelves | *A low stool for resting your feet | A small cupboard for dishes | A large table for dinner
exercise: The word footstool is built from two smaller words. Which two? | foot and stoop | *foot and stool | foot and stove | food and stool
exercise: In the Bible, God says «the earth is my footstool». What does footstool mean here? | A kind of wooden bridge | *Something under God's feet, showing that he is greater than the world | A low hill near a church | A stool God sits on to eat his dinner
test: «No indeed!», jumps on the footstool and braids up her hair «for fear that the mouse should run up it». What does the Woman fear? | Losing the footstool | *The mouse running up her hair | Being too hot by the fire | Rain on the roof
test: Which meaning of footstool is used in «the earth is my footstool»? | A tall chair with arms | A stool in the kitchen for the cook | *Something under someone's feet, showing power | A low stool for resting your feet
exam: Using «The Woman jumps onto a footstool», where would she put her feet? | Under the table | On the roof | In the bath | *On the footstool
